' (VB) generated by tools/gen_gl.py: do not edit. glad (3rdparty/glad: glad.h, glad.c) for the GL
' functions and constants lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp uses: GL 1.0 / 1.1 functions are
' opengl32.dll's exports, every later one a wrapper that calls its entry point (glad_glX, loaded
' by gladLoadGLLoader / gladLoadGLES2Loader through the backend's getGLGetProcAddress) with
' DispCallFunc. Pointers, enums and integers are ByVal Long (an address is a VarPtr), GLfloat is
' Single, a const GLchar * is a String (an ANSI copy; vbNullString = nullptr). A call to a function
' that is not loaded raises an error.
